{:edb/db-before-t 1706 :edb/db-after-t 1707 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535019 50 #inst "2026-10-08T14:47:24.047Z" 13194139535019 true] [17592186087640 1020 #edb/ref 17592186327124 13194139535019 true] [17592186087640 1020 #edb/ref 17592186327131 13194139535019 true] [17592186087640 1020 #edb/ref 17592186327138 13194139535019 true] [17592186327124 1017 #edb/ref 17592186327125 13194139535019 true] [17592186327124 1089 "q-127899" 13194139535019 true] [17592186327124 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535019 true] [17592186327124 1100 "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}k-1 & k-1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $k.$" 13194139535019 true] [17592186327124 1113 #uuid "d7637210-9ef1-5fcb-8a52-1b1182a7f30d" 13194139535019 true] [17592186327124 1145 "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(k-1)\\cdot (-1)-(k-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-k+1-3k+3 \\\\  & =-4k+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4k+4 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $k$ is $k=1.$" 13194139535019 true] [17592186327125 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327126 13194139535019 true] [17592186327125 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327127 13194139535019 true] [17592186327125 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327128 13194139535019 true] [17592186327125 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327129 13194139535019 true] [17592186327125 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327130 13194139535019 true] [17592186327125 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535019 true] [17592186327125 1041 "selection" 13194139535019 true] [17592186327125 1104 #edb/ref 17592186327127 13194139535019 true] [17592186327125 1110 #uuid "e9fc1327-c2a1-56a5-9234-41287bcce160" 13194139535019 true] [17592186327126 1034 "k=3" 13194139535019 true] [17592186327126 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535019 true] [17592186327126 1111 #uuid "3609191a-ea7f-5f46-b68d-43403d91dce0" 13194139535019 true] [17592186327127 1034 "